# TerritoryKit core policy

- Before substantive changes: read `git status`, current branch, and `docs/ai-handoff/README.md`.
- Follow established package boundaries (`scripts/check-package-boundaries.mjs`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`). Do not invent APIs or packages.
- Prefer repository evidence (code, tests, `reports/`, ADRs) over assumptions. Mark unverified claims explicitly.
- Keep diffs small and reviewable. Do not modify unrelated files or dirty working-tree content owned by the user.
- Never claim tests or CI passed unless you executed them in this session and report the command output.
- Preserve stable territory IDs, source provenance, and geometry hashes unless an explicit migration review authorizes change.
- Distinguish: registered providers, downloaded bytes, imported geometry, effective gameplay geometry, built artifacts, hosted delivery, and consumer cache state.
- Do not merge, deploy, publish to npm, or promote datasets without explicit user permission.
- Untracked local files (e.g. root `AGENTS.md` from Turbo) must not be staged or overwritten without authorization.
- For geospatial or release work, read `docs/ai-handoff/CURRENT_MILESTONE.md` and `NEXT_ACTIONS.md` before implementing.
